course: dictionary
lesson: 13244
title: Rocks and deep time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Geological means to do with geology, the science of the Earth's rocks, soil and layers, and how they formed and changed. The ending -al often means "to do with", as in natural or musical. So a geological word is about rocks and the Earth.
explain: Geologists read the story of the land from its layers. «The geological map shows where the chalk and the granite rocks are.» You can guess that a map like this helps people know which rocks lie under the ground.
explain: Geology also counts time in very big numbers. «Mountains and canyons took geological time to form.» That means they did not appear in an afternoon. They took millions of years, so the clue is the word time.
fact: Geology is the science of the Earth's rocks, soil, layers, and how they formed and changed.
fact: «Geological» means to do with geology.
fact: «Geological time» means very long stretches of Earth's history, millions of years long.
fact: A «geological map» shows which rocks are where.
fact: A «geological feature» is a part of the land, such as a cliff or canyon, made by rock and time.
exercise: «The river carved a deep canyon over geological time.» What does geological time mean? | A few minutes after lunch | A time for holidays | One school day | *Millions of years of Earth's history
exercise: «The geological map showed where the chalk and granite rocks lay.» What does a geological map show? | The number of birds in a park | Where the best ice cream shops are | How fast the wind blows | *Which rocks are where
exercise: Which word in «The geological survey found a new kind of stone.» means to do with rocks and the Earth? | survey | stone | found | *geological
test: «Scientists studied the cliffs to learn about a geological feature.» What is a geological feature? | A type of school lesson | *A part of the land, such as a cliff or canyon, made by rock and time | A new kind of cake | A film about the weather
test: Maya says, «Mountains took geological time to form.» What does this tell us? | They were built by people last week | They formed in one day | They appeared after lunch | *They took millions of years to form
exam: Ella says a geological survey is just a school test. Why is she wrong? | A survey is a map of the sea | A survey is a kind of cake | *A survey studies the rocks and land of an area | A survey is a quiz about maths
